# Hump Test - BONANZA's HUMP test course (SPEC.md 128.44), built only by the BZHUMP=1 knob (make BUILD=<tree>
# BZHUMP=1 bonanzadisk).  NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES and makes it the pathway's pad 0,
# so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.  A hump is FIELD cells that rise ABOVE
# the plate round them: a raised cosine, 6 px (LOW) or 10 px (HIGH) at its crest, the plate's own height at its
# edge - a round DOME on the 2 x 2 cells round a cell corner, or a RIDGE along an axis (domed ends, or `open`
# ends against walls: a speed bump no ball rolls round).
#
# A level plate at 2 units.  From the start (the pads for each ball on its left):
#  - THE LOW HUMPS (the middle): three 6 px domes and a 6 px ridge every ball rolls over from a standstill;
#  - THE SPEED BUMP (east): a bridge 2 wide, a HIGH open ridge across it.  Glass climbs it
#    from rest, rubber with a cell of run-up, steel only with a long run (the corridor's 5 cells) - from a
#    standstill at its foot steel STALLS and rolls back.  Its goal is exit 0;
#  - THE HIDE (front): a HIGH dome with a glass pad behind it and the exit 1 goal beyond: the dome hides part of
#    the pad and of a ball rolling behind it, never all of either for more than a ball length (128.44.4).
course HUMP "Hump Test"
width 128
origin 448
ball rubber

floor rect 4 4 16 20 flat 2
pad rubber 5 18
pad steel 6 18
pad glass 7 18
start 5 16

# THE LOW HUMPS
hump 8 8 2
hump 12 10 2
hump 8 12 2
hump 11 14 2 along x 3

# THE SPEED BUMP: the bridge (x 16 - 26, y 6 - 7) over the void, the open ridge across it at x 21 - 22 (its ends
# over the void, so no ball rolls round it)
floor rect 16 6 27 8 flat 2
hump 22 6 2 along y 2 height 10 open
goal tile 26 6 flat 2

# THE HIDE: a HIGH dome at (13, 18), a glass pad behind it at (11, 16)
hump 13 18 2 height 10
pad glass 11 16
floor rect 16 16 20 20 flat 2
goal tile 18 17 flat 2 exit 1

clock 14 5
target 60
way 5 16
way 10 10
way 14 7
way 20 7
way 26 6
